+### [VMRF (View Matching Neural Radiance Fields)](12630-vmrf-view-matching-neural-radiance-fields.md)
+VMRF is a method for novel view synthesis that learns Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) representations without prior knowledge of camera poses or hand-crafted camera pose distributions. It distinguishes itself from pose-free alternatives like GNeRF by estimating relative pose transformations via view matching using unbalanced optimal transport, rather than estimating absolute poses directly from images. This approach makes VMRF robust to out-of-dataset views and eliminates the need for accurate, hand-crafted camera pose distributions required by inversion networks.
+
+### [Neural SAR Surface Reconstruction via Inverse Rendering](12668-neural-sar-surface-reconstruction-via-inverse-rendering.md)
+A method to reconstruct a Digital Surface Model (DSM) and backscattering coefficient map from Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) images by minimizing the difference between observed SAR intensities and synthesized intensities using a differentiable rendering model. It models elevation Z and backscattering B within a bounding box using an MLP, reducing sampling degrees of freedom from 3D volume to 2D surface.
